# ⚖️ Clause IQ — AI-Powered Contract Risk Analyzer

Clause IQ is a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) app that lets you upload a legal contract and ask natural-language questions about it — termination clauses, indemnity risk, penalties, auto-renewal terms, and more. It retrieves the most relevant clauses from the document and uses an LLM to answer your question while flagging potentially risky language.

## ✨ Features

- 📄 Upload contracts in **PDF, DOCX, or TXT**
- 🔍 Ask free-form questions (e.g. *"What are the termination clauses?"*)
- ⚠️ Automatic **risk keyword detection** (liability, termination, indemnity, penalty, renewal)
- 🎛️ Adjustable **retrieval depth (Top-K)** and **risk sensitivity**
- 📂 Source-chunk attribution for every answer
- ⬇️ Downloadable **risk analysis report**
- 🧠 Powered by **Mistral AI** for generation and **OpenAI embeddings** for retrieval

## 🏗️ Tech Stack

| Component | Technology |

| UI | Streamlit |
| Orchestration | LangChain |
| Vector Store | ChromaDB |
| Embeddings | OpenAI (`text-embedding-3-small`) |
| LLM | Mistral AI |
| Document Parsing | PyPDFLoader, Docx2txtLoader, TextLoader |

## 📁 Project Structure

'''
clause-iq/
├── app.py              # Streamlit UI
├── config.py           # API keys, model + chunking config
├── document_loader.py  # Loads and splits PDF/DOCX/TXT files
├── ingest.py           # Builds the vector store from a folder of contracts
├── retriever.py        # Wraps the vector store as a retriever
├── risk_analyzer.py    # RAG chain + risk-aware prompt template
├── vector_store.py     # Chroma embedding + persistence logic
└── requirements.txt
'''

## 📊 Dataset

Clause IQ doesn't ship with a bundled dataset — it's designed to analyze *any contract you upload* at runtime. For building and testing the RAG pipeline (ingestion, chunking, retrieval quality), the following publicly available legal-contract sources work well:

-1. [CUAD – Contract Understanding Atticus Dataset](https://www.atticusprojectai.org/cuad) — 510 real commercial contracts (NDAs, licensing, employment, M&A, etc.) sourced from *SEC EDGAR* filings, expert-annotated across 41 clause categories. Great for testing retrieval and risk-clause detection at scale. Available on [Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/datasets/theatticusproject/cuad-qa) and [Zenodo](https://zenodo.org/record/4595826).

-2.[LegalBench-RAG](https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.10343)** — a benchmark combining CUAD, ContractNLI (NDAs), MAUD (M&A agreements), and PrivacyQA, useful if you want to evaluate retrieval accuracy with ground-truth Q&A pairs.

> ⚠️ Note: publicly filed contracts (e.g. via EDGAR/CUAD) are legally public documents, but always double-check licensing terms before redistributing any dataset you package with the project.

## ⚙️ Setup

```bash
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd clause-iq
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Create a `.env` file in the project root:

'''
OPENAI_API_KEY = your_openai_key
MISTRAL_API_KEY = your_mistral_key
MISTRAL_MODEL = open-mistral-7b
'''

## 🚀 Usage

a. Ingest contracts into the vector store

Place one or more contract files in the folder pointed to by `DATA_DIR` in `config.py`, then run:

```bash
python ingest.py
```

b. Launch the app

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

c..Analyze

Upload a contract, type a question (or use one of the sidebar examples), and click ** Analyze Contract ** to get an answer, flagged risk areas, and source citations.

